  "published": "2026-08-03T17:09:38.593Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v2.0.0-preview.6: PREVIEW - Add EnumerateDirectoriesAsync (list subdirectories) and GetFileInfoAsync (extended file metadata: altname, create/access/write/change times, attributes, and alternate data streams via smbclient's \"allinfo\" command) to IFileHandler/ISmbClientFileHandler, addressing GitHub issues #2 and #3. New SmbSharp.Models.SmbFileInfo result type. v2.0.0-preview.5: PREVIEW - Fix session-pool WriteFileAsync failing under WSL: pooled ExecuteAsync did not translate embedded Windows temp-file paths (e.g. \"put C:\\...\\file remote\") to their WSL /mnt/<drive>/... equivalents before sending to smbclient, unlike the non-pooled path. v2.0.0-preview.4: PREVIEW - Fix root cause of session pool hang: smbclient never emits its interactive prompt \"smb: \\> \" at all (not just buffered) unless stdin is a TTY. Output buffering fixes alone (stdbuf) could not solve this. Now invokes smbclient through \"script -qec\" to allocate a real pseudo-terminal, restoring prompt output; verified end-to-end against a live share, including natively inside Linux (WSL) with no wsl.exe relay involved. v2.0.0-preview.3: PREVIEW - Fix session pool still hanging: line-buffering (stdbuf -oL) does not flush smbclient's interactive prompt \"smb: \\> \" because it has no trailing newline. Switched to fully-unbuffered stdbuf -o0 -e0. v2.0.0-preview.2: PREVIEW - Fix persistent session pool hanging indefinitely: smbclient fully buffers stdout when not attached to a TTY, so the interactive prompt/banner could sit unflushed and never reach the reader. Now invokes smbclient via stdbuf -oL -eL to force line-buffered output. v2.0.0-preview.1: PREVIEW - Add persistent session pool support (UseSessionPool option) to avoid re-authenticating (full connect/negotiate/Kerberos handshake) on every smbclient call. Keeps a small pool of persistent, authenticated smbclient sessions per share; transparently recreates and retries once if a session dies mid-operation. v1.1.2: Repackage of v1.1.1 fixes with clean build (previous package contained stale binaries). Fix EnumerateFilesAsync on smbclient path: include files with any attribute (not just Archive), correctly parse filenames containing spaces, return empty list for empty directories instead of throwing, and include hidden dot-files. v1.1.0: Add macOS support (smbclient), WSL smbclient support on Windows (opt-in), and sample console app.",
